+Stdio stderr drainage is owned by its connection. Dropping a failed initializer, completed isolated search or replaced search requests cancellation of that reader; Tokio releases its pipe on cancellation, without waiting for a descendant to close its writer or killing unrelated descendants. Repeated-search pipe tests distinguish cancellation from ordinary EOF.
+
@@ -36,0 +39,4 @@ On Windows→SSH Ubuntu the TUI reads **Ubuntu-side** Codex Home, shell cwd and
+Git identity preserves whitespace, carriage returns and embedded newlines: only the final protocol LF is removed. Unrepresentable UTF-8, missing directories and a root that does not contain the current cwd fail closed. Review editor launch rechecks the source cwd and root containment; presentation sanitization never rewrites the file argument. Same-user concurrent filesystem replacement is not claimed race-free.
+
+Ordinary Git probes retain at most 2 MiB stdout, 64 KiB stderr and 10,000 status entries, under the existing three-second deadline. Byte or entry overflow, malformed NUL framing and unrepresentable paths are errors, not a truncated clean repository. Review diff display may still explicitly truncate at its existing 2 MiB limit. Detailed change lists are immutable shared slices across threads on one cwd and planning snapshots; per-thread identity/summary remains separate. These are data budgets and sharing guarantees, not a global RSS certification.
+
